@startuml experiment_submit_dispatch
!theme plain
hide footbox
skinparam maxMessageSize 300
skinparam wrapWidth 380
title Experiment submit (2/3) — dispatcher: claim, spawn, timeout and completion

participant "db.py\n(SQLite WAL)" as DB
participant "Dispatcher\n(asyncio loop)" as Disp
participant "Runner\n(subprocess)" as Runner

== Dispatch ==
note over Disp: _loop body wrapped in try/except —\na single hung/erroring experiment can never wedge\nthe queue (F-2.10-01); logs and continues on the next tick.
Disp -> Disp: _loop: poll every 1s
Disp -> DB: dequeue_next()\n(One atomic UPDATE...RETURNING,\nqueued -> running + started_at, gated on\nnot-paused + no other 'running' row)
DB --> Disp: experiment (spec_json, id) — already 'running' in DB
Disp -> Disp: parse spec_json -> kind ("spec" | "script")\nderive per-experiment timeout from budget\n(_compute_timeout_seconds)
note right of Disp: mkdir / write spec / open _stdout.log\nall inside the same try/except as the spawn below\n — a filesystem error marks failed,\nit cannot kill the dispatcher task

alt kind == "script"
    Disp -> Disp: write user_script.py
    Disp -> Runner: Popen([python, user_script.py],\n  cwd=<experiment-dir>, env=PYTHONPATH+=DEAP_PROJECT_ROOT,\n  start_new_session/CREATE_NEW_PROCESS_GROUP,\n  stdout=_stdout.log)
else kind == "spec" (default)
    Disp -> Runner: Popen([python, -m, deap_pettingzoo.service.runner,\n  ~--spec-file <path>, ~--experiment-dir <dir>],\n  start_new_session/CREATE_NEW_PROCESS_GROUP,\n  stdout=_stdout.log)
end
Disp -> DB: set_pid(id, pid)\n(claim already set status/started_at; this only attaches the pid)
note right of Disp: logger.info "Experiment {id} running (pid, log, timeout)"\n(diagnostic log — see sequence_logging_pipeline.puml)\n Own process group/session so a timeout/cancel\ncan kill the whole tree, not just the immediate process

== Completion ==
Disp -> Runner: asyncio.wait_for(proc.wait(), timeout)
alt timeout expires
    Disp -> Runner: terminate_group(proc)\n(taskkill /T on Windows; killpg on POSIX)\nthen force-kill after a grace period
    Disp -> DB: set_failed(id, "...timed out...")
    note right of Disp: logger.error; the next queued experiment\nis picked up on the dispatcher's very next tick
else proc exits in time
    note right of Disp: kind=="script": synthesise _result.json from exit code\n+ run_dirs discovered via rglob("manifest.json")
    Disp -> Disp: read _result.json
    Disp -> DB: exit=0 -> set_completed\n≠0 -> set_failed
    note right of Disp: completed -> logger.info\nfailed -> logger.error "Experiment {id} failed: ..."
end
Disp --> DB: done

note over DB
  Fragment of <i>sequence_experiment_submit.puml</i>.
  Steps and participants outside this
  fragment are omitted.
end note

@enduml
